## JANISSARY {{VERSION}}

Code-freeze release. Functionally complete; frozen to prevent regressions. Architectural work
continues in 8.x.

### Benchmark status

No scored performance claim is made in this release. The pre-registered methodology is in
`BENCHMARK.md` (v7.2.0, frozen 2026-09-28). Scored results and run artifacts will be published
as a separate benchmark announcement once committed to `benchmark/track_a/runs/`.

### What's in the box

- **Deduplication / grouping.** DVWA run: 8 CRITICAL signals grouped into 1 finding.
- **WAF evasion evidence.** Live ModSecurity: pacer backed off to 30.0s across 38 events
  (backoff behavior observed, not a claimed bypass).
- **Framework-specific SQLi payloads.** Paren-closing payloads verified live.

### Install

    docker pull {{IMAGE_REPO}}:{{VERSION}}
    pip install {{PKG}}=={{VERSION}}

`:latest` points at digest `{{IMAGE_DIGEST}}` — same as `:{{VERSION}}`.

### Known limitations

- **SPA catch-all false positives** (Issue #1). 39 FPs observed on a Node SPA in our Juice Shop run.
- **401 abort** (Issue #2). 401 aborts the scan for that path; may mask auth-gated findings.
- **Pathtraver recall 0.049-0.308.** Not a supported detection class in 7.x.
- **Framework-wrapped SQLi can be missed.** Juice Shop search endpoint not flagged in our run —
  payload-set limitation, scoped to 8.x with Issue #4.

### Deferred to 8.x

- Issue #4 — generalize the six-oracle pattern to close the misattribution class.
- `--mode ci` — fast, unpaced mode for trusted CI/CD.
- Payload-set generalization for framework-wrapped queries.
- Scored benchmark announcement (see Benchmark status above).

